> <tr> <td>CPCCCA3017</td> <td>Install exterior cladding</td> <td>40</td> <td>ELECTIVES</td> </tr> <tr> <td>CPCCCA3012</td> <td>Frame and fit wet area fixtures</td> <td>60</td> <td>ELECTIVES</td> </tr> <tr> <td>CPCCCA3014</td> <td>Construct and install bulkheads</td> <td>60</td> <td>ELECTIVES</td> </tr> <tr> <td>CPCCCA3027</td> <td>Set up, operate and maintain indirect action powder-actuated power tools</td> <td>40</td> <td>ELECTIVES</td> </tr> <tr> <td colspan="4"><strong>TERM 7</strong></td> </tr> <tr> <td>CPCCCA3016</td> <td>Construct, assemble and install timber external stairs</td> <td>60</td> <td>CORE</td> </tr> <tr> <td>CPCCCA3008</td> <td>Construct eaves</td> <td>40</td> <td>CORE</td> </tr> <tr> <td>CPCCCA3005</td> <td>Construct ceiling frames</td> <td>40</td> <td>CORE</td> </tr> <tr> <td>CPCCCA3024</td> <td>Install lining, panelling and moulding</td> <td>60</td> <td>CORE</td> </tr> <tr> <td colspan="4"><strong>TERM 8</strong></td> </tr> <tr> <td>CPCCCA3003</td> <td>Install flooring systems</td> <td>100</td> <td>CORE</td> </tr> <tr> <td>CPCCCA3007</td> <td>Construct pitched roofs</td> <td>60</td> <td>CORE</td> </tr> <tr> <td>CPCCOM1012</td> <td>Work effectively and sustainably in the construction industry</td> <td>40</td> <td>0</td> </tr> <tr> <td colspan="2">Total</td> <td>1600</td> <td></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div><h4>Pathway</h4><p><strong>Upon completion of the Certificate III in Carpentry, graduates can pursue various career pathways, including:</strong></p> <ul> <li>Carpenter</li> <li>Formwork Carpenter</li> <li>Residential or Commercial Builder’s Assistant</li> <li>Shopfitter</li> <li>Joiner</li> </ul> <p> </p>',
